Fine-tuning
-------------------
Fine-tuning = retraining the model further on your own data, so it permanently absorbs new patterns/knowledge into its weights — without needing that data fed to 
it again later (unlike RAG).

Fine-tuning applies to the base model itself (Llama3/Claude) — not to RAG.

Clear distinction:

+-----------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|                 | Fine-tuning                                                  | RAG                                                          |
+-----------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| What changes    | The model's actual weights get updated (real training)       | Nothing about the model changes — it stays completely frozen |
+-----------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| What you're     | Retraining Llama3 further on new data to                     | Feeding external documents as temporary context at           |
| doing           | permanently bake in new knowledge/behavior                   | question-time                                                |
+-----------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| Result          | A new version of the model (e.g., Llama3 ->                  | Same original Llama3, just answering with extra              |
|                 | your-custom-llama3)                                          | reference material each time                                 |
+-----------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| Effort/cost     | Needs GPU compute, training pipeline, real ML                | What you built today — Python script + vector DB,            |
|                 | engineering                                                  | no training involved                                         |
+-----------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+

Practical result of fine-tuning (example for you):

If you fine-tuned Llama3 on your Worldpay Jenkins pipeline docs:

• It would start answering pipeline questions confidently without needing RAG lookup
  — the knowledge becomes baked into the weights

• But it might also forget some of its general Llama3 knowledge in the process
  (this is a real risk called "catastrophic forgetting") if not done carefully

The parallel:

+--------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| RAG                                        | Fine-tuning                                                  |
+--------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| Add more files to docs/ folder             | Add more training examples to your fine-tuning dataset       |
+--------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| Run python rag.py ingest                   | Run a retraining job (GPU-based training script)             |
+--------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| ChromaDB gets updated with new embeddings  | Model's actual weights get updated                           |
+--------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| Llama3 itself stays unchanged              | Llama3's weights literally change — new version created      |
+--------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| Takes seconds/minutes                      | Takes hours/days, needs GPU compute                          |
+--------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+

